From fcbfb53710cc3befe3350486d54a68ee41d4b426 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoaoZaokk <joaozaogb@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:06:09 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Run quantized text encoders with their quantized matmul

The float32 upcast of every CLIP force casts each weight, so a quantized
text encoder saved VRAM and no time. After its weights load, a text
encoder whose layers can run their quantized matmul on the load device
skips the upcast and encodes inside use_quantized_matmul, as generate
already does. Layers marked full_precision_matrix_mult, or in a format the
device cannot run, keep the old path. --disable-quantized-text-encoder
restores it everywhere.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
